l-offs it fell 30% in the 2020 crash, 40% in the 2022 bear market and 76% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $88.59 (margin of safety -0%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 6%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $54.72 to $140 (P10-P90).","Multiples send mixed signals against Real Estate peers: cheaper on P/FCF 13.1 vs 17.8, richer on P/E 35.6 vs 23.6 and EV/EBITDA 23.2 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 28% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 7.6% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 21 covering analysts target $93.50 on average, 6% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% earns above the cost of capital of 6.8%, but the 1pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.95).","It converts 67% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is a concern: high accruals (-8.3% of assets).","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 67%.","Operating margin is running 25pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.7% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 8.8x net debt to EBITDA ($99.0M of cash against $24.3B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.1x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.01 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.26 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -15.2% over 3 years, -6.1% over 5 years and 1.5% over 10 years, so the decline is deepening, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 15%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 15.0% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.5% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.63 (orders lagging sales), a backlog worth 10% of annual revenue, deferred revenue down 60% and FFO growth of 0.0% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (4.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year.","It returns 5.6% a year to shareholders (0.1% in buybacks and 4.8% in dividends).","It pays out 171% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 1,500 employees, each generates about $2.8M of revenue, 1.2x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 6.0% a year.","That works out to $1.9M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.0M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $49K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":44,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety and too few checks pass (conviction 44); it becomes a buy below $75.30.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 40, gates 11/24)","FCF margin 67.4%","P/FCF 13.1x vs sector 17.8x","Operating margin expanding 1.5%/yr","Returns 5.6% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 0% above fair value of $88.59","Revenue shrank 6.1%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 8.8x","Interest coverage only 2.1x","P/E 35.6x vs sector 23.6x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","too few checks pass (conviction 44)"],"buy_below":75.3,"vc":{"base":88.59,"base_src":"dcf","bear":54.72,"bull":139.79,"alt_median":103.98,"n_alt":1,"gap":0.1286,"dispersion":0.0604,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"CCI","date":"2026-11-06"}